dsh-ssh-logs README · Use in conversations：Type `@` in the composer and select an SSH server:

```text
@production run tail -n 300 /var/log/nginx/access.log
@staging run grep -nF request-id=abc123 /srv/app/backend.log
```

The picker inserts `@server-name`. Use the root-based log tools for read-only servers; general commands require read-write authorization. Credentials never enter conversation context.

dsh-ssh-logs README · 对话使用：在输入框输入 `@`，选择某个 SSH 服务器：

```text
@production 执行 tail -n 300 /var/log/nginx/access.log
@staging 执行 grep -nF request-id=abc123 /srv/app/backend.log
```

选择后会插入 `@服务器名`。只读服务器使用日志根目录工具，通用命令需要读写授权；密码不会进入对话上下文。
